# Development Workflow

> Extends [git-workflow.mdc](./git-workflow.mdc) with the implementation flow
> for this dashboard.

## Delivery Sequence

1. Read the canonical guidance in `AGENTS.md`, `docs/RULES.md`,
   `docs/CONTEXT.md`, `docs/TECH_STACK.md`, and the active ticket under
   `docs/tickets/`. For UI work, also apply
   [`.cursor/rules/web/design-system.mdc`](../web/design-system.mdc).
2. Plan non-trivial work and identify the smallest complete vertical slice.
3. Preserve Nx boundaries: `apps/dashboard`, `apps/gateway`, and
   `apps/producer` may depend on reusable `packages/*`; packages never depend
   on apps.
4. Implement the active ticket slice before broad test construction.
5. Validate changed boundaries and run focused checks proportional to risk.
6. Review the actual diff with evidence, then follow the git workflow.

## Project Tooling

- Use Bun for installs and command execution, Nx for project tasks and
  boundaries, and Biome for formatting and linting once scaffolded.
- Use Docker Compose for local ClickHouse and Redis.
- Use primary vendor documentation when behavior is version-sensitive.
- Do not add a dependency or abstraction without a confirmed capability gap.
- Do not scaffold, install tooling, or create infrastructure outside the active
  plan phase.

## Testing Sequence

Testing is deferred, not omitted. Final risk-based QA uses Jest with React
Testing Library for selected unit and integration seams and Playwright for
critical browser journeys. Add an earlier focused test only when it materially
reduces risk around a hard contract, parser, worker protocol, or regression.

Global validation belongs to the final validation phase unless the user asks
for it earlier.
